#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151820 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152299 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "be45dab5-8dcc-5820-9ada-fa57dd060d37" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions With Addition and Subtraction"}] :question/id #uuid "fc9992be-d6e0-569b-b0a9-7ff40a8c0e22" :question/math-academy-id "e-12831" :question/problem "Evaluate $-7 + 3.1 - 5$." :question/worked-solution "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nWe add and subtract, from left to right:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-7 + 3.1 - 5 &=  \\\\\n(-7 + 3.1) - 5 &=  \\\\\n- 3.9 - 5 &=  \\\\\n&= - 8.9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151821 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152300 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3656cdd-e02d-5ce5-805c-8c76cc0f5996" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions With Multiplication and Division"}] :question/id #uuid "9d5382d3-5153-5457-ae03-26736f3a123a" :question/math-academy-id "e-12832" :question/problem "What is the value of $2 \\div 6 \\times (-5)$?" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nWe divide and multiply, from left to right:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2 \\div 6 \\cdot (-5) &=  \\\\\n(2 \\div 6) \\cdot (-5) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{2}{6} \\cdot (-5) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot (-5) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot ((-5))/(1) &=  \\\\\n(1 \\cdot (-5))/(3 \\cdot 1) &=  \\\\\n&= - \\frac{5}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151822 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152301 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40c77bba-95b6-5f8d-876d-3eb0b0905d6d" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Numerical Expressions Containing Multiple Operations"}] :question/id #uuid "216c39cc-456d-5bf8-abbc-2860ab3ebb43" :question/math-academy-id "e-12833" :question/problem "Evaluate $-2 + 6 \\div (-10)$." :question/worked-solution "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nFirst, we divide:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2 + 6 \\div (-10) &=  \\\\\n- 2 + (6 \\div (-10)) &=  \\\\\n&= - 2 + (-0.6)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we add:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2 + (-0.6) &= -2.6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151823 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152302 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b48ae5a6-0426-58c1-ab88-10b748043f6f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions Containing Parentheses"}] :question/id #uuid "1fedcc75-84fe-5f3f-9555-896493c91232" :question/math-academy-id "e-12834" :question/problem "What is the value of $\\left(-3 + 6 \\right) \\div \\dfrac{4}{3} - \\dfrac{1}{4}$?" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nFirst, we perform the operation inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(-3 + 6) \\div \\frac{4}{3} - \\frac{1}{4} &=  \\\\\n&= 3 \\div \\frac{4}{3} - \\frac{1}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we divide:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3 \\div \\frac{4}{3} - \\frac{1}{4} &=  \\\\\n(3 \\div \\frac{4}{3}) - \\frac{1}{4} &=  \\\\\n(\\frac{3}{1} \\div \\frac{4}{3}) - \\frac{1}{4} &=  \\\\\n(\\frac{3}{1} \\cdot \\frac{3}{4}) - \\frac{1}{4} &=  \\\\\n\\frac{3 \\cdot 3}{1 \\cdot 4} - \\frac{1}{4} &=  \\\\\n&= \\frac{9}{4} - \\frac{1}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we subtract:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{9}{4} - \\frac{1}{4} &=  \\\\\n\\frac{9 - 1}{4} &=  \\\\\n\\frac{8}{4} &=  \\\\\n8 \\div 4 &=  \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
